Subject: [PATCH] OSCORE: verify a request without replay check or replay-window update

Add coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu_ext(session, pdu, flags); coap_oscore_decrypt_pdu()
becomes a wrapper with flags 0 and its behaviour is unchanged.

With COAP_OSCORE_DECRYPT_NO_REPLAY (requests only) a protected request is
decrypted and, in group mode, its countersignature verified, as for any
request, but:
- RFC 8613 Section 8.2 Step 3 (replay check) is skipped, and the Recipient
  Context replay state (last_seq, sliding_window, rollback values,
  initial_state) is neither read nor written, on success or failure;
- no Appendix B.1.2 / B.2 processing, no association for the Token, no
  change to session->recipient_ctx / b_2_step / doing_b_1_2;
- nothing is sent: no error response, no ACK.

This is the processing that draft-ietf-core-observe-multicast-notifications
Section 9.3.1 requires for the phantom registration request 'ph_req' that a
client rebuilds from an informative response ("MUST NOT perform any replay
check", "MUST NOT update the Replay Window", "MUST NOT deliver ... MUST NOT
take any action in the Token space"). It is a per-call flag: replay
protection stays in force for every message processed without it.

Applies on top of patches/libcoap/0001-0004 (needed for group-mode
verification at all: 0004).
